s9-3-p75 : Block
s9-3-p75 = prose (cons "A *static* residual call to the evaluator can remain where code or environment is not known at specialization time. A dynamically computed type family, closure, or face condition does not itself force such a call: it can be compiled directly whenever the corresponding machine relation has been constructed. A *dynamic* exit occurs when a direct block's own stated premise fails, for example an arithmetic fast path that assumes a result fits in a machine word. Its correctness requires either a proved continuation map from the current direct state to an evaluator configuration, or a justified restart of the computation." nil)
